<title>ITALY: Olivetti 1996 net loss 916 billion lire.</title>
<headline>Olivetti 1996 net loss 916 billion lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's information technology group Olivetti on Tuesday reported a net loss for 1996 of 915 billion lire ($538.3 million) as annual sales fell 14.6 percent to 8.304 trillion lire.</p>
<p>A company statment said the group's net financial requirement at end-1996 was 2.197 trillion lire, while adding that first quarter 1997 results were in line with budget projections. It said that the parent company Olivetti SpA had set a extraordinary general meeting to approve a proposal to reduce the share capital.</p>
</text>
